\title{enzKinet2: models for enzyme kinetics}
\description{
enzKinet2 simulates, fits and plots 14 models of enzyme and binding
kinetics. It is the engine behind EKA2, the enzyme kinetics web app at
\url{https://eka.nz}.

The package has six functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=simulate_data]{simulate_data()}} makes noisy data from a model and parameter values.
\item \code{\link[=make_curve]{make_curve()}} makes a model's curve (dense, noise-free values), with an
optional parameter uncertainty envelope.
\item \code{\link[=fit_model]{fit_model()}} fits a model to data and returns parameter estimates,
confidence intervals and fit statistics.
\item \code{\link[=make_plot]{make_plot()}} plots data and curves, with or without a linearising
transformation.
\item \code{\link[=make_residual_plot]{make_residual_plot()}} plots the residuals of data from a model.
\item \code{\link[=update_plot_curve]{update_plot_curve()}} replaces the curve in an existing plot.
}

The models, their parameters and their variables are listed in
\link{model_registry}.

Guides, worked examples and the EKA2 user guide are at
\url{https://eka.nz/docs}.
}
